+# Ordered cell-voltage readout
+
+Original `new120:rx-012` asks for equal-magnitude opposite-sign readings after reversing zinc concentration-cell terminals, compared with actual zinc activities. The unchanged script uses100mL water and1gZn on each side, with0.0001mol versus0.01molZnSO4. The saved abf-source review reports+0.040039V in both orders: C1 FAIL/C2 PASS. It remains preserved and unqualified.
+
+`displacement::cell` already computes admitted half-cell Nernst potentials, then sorts electrodes into spontaneous anode/cathode order. Its positive `Cell.volts` represents spontaneous chemical driving force, so swapping requested leads loses the sign. The repair adds `Cell::terminal_volts()` and carries the original vessel order in optional `CellVoltage.terminals {first, second, volts}`. The signed reading is `E(second)-E(first)`: first is the negative/reference lead, second the positive lead. It uses the existing resolved activities and temperature. Spontaneous electrode roles, magnitude, standard voltage, equation and notation remain unchanged. No new species, activity law, thermodynamic constant, kinetic parameter or stock is added.
+
+The actual `Operator::Cell` path emits the ordered readout. EN/DE/FR rendering states lead order and signed voltage; the CLI semantic scalar adapter exposes `terminal_volts` separately from the legacy spontaneous `volts`. Historical events deserialize with no terminal reading and serialize without fabricated order. The acid-metal estimate route is unchanged and does not gain a resolved-activity claim.
+
+Four core controls cover reversed leads with unchanged stock/roles, unresolved/equal/invalid-activity refusal, historical JSON round-trip and EN/DE/FR signed rendering. The existing CLI scalar guard is preserved and extended to require the additional signed field only when order exists. These fixtures test readout behavior; they do not supply scientific observations or qualify the original.
+
+Formatting, diff checks, locale placeholder checks and i18n lint pass. Rust compile/runtime tests are **UNEXECUTED** after the single Cycle73 admission refused load6.202148 while lock, memory and reserve passed. No second admission, native original replay, new validation job or PR is issued. Next bounded acceptance is `cargo test --locked -p kerotakis-core --test cell_terminal_polarity`, the CLI semantic scalar guard, and subsequently an admitted exact-source unchanged-original positive/refusal review with actual zinc activities and complete stock/charge/thermal-state checks. Ordinary source/platform/fleet acceptance remains required before integration. No golden or original predicate is weakened or blessed here.
+
+Coverage stays431/468 originals,435 catalog objects,37 remaining. GS007's two524 projection controls remain unexecuted and its C2 failure remains separate. PR884ee027 stays DRAFT; this source branch does not amend it or authorize a merge or Apple action.
